From: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:58:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 09/12] logging: add runtime extension enrichment support

Add support for runtime enrichment of event extension payloads.

During log creation, registered runtime metadata providers may
contribute extension payloads that are consolidated into the
existing _EXTENSIONS transport object. The resulting data is
processed using the normal event extension framework and requires
no changes to event producers.

User supplied extension data takes precedence over runtime generated
payloads, allowing platform specific enrichment to coexist with
explicitly provided extension metadata.

This infrastructure enables OEM specific extension data, such as
CPER OEM metadata, to be automatically populated while preserving
the existing extension transport, serialization, restore, and
lifecycle management flows.

Change-Id: Ie5dc1a68844e8e342b13fa74ebf5f8bc40d8749d
Signed-off-by: Jayanth Othayoth <ojayanth@gmail.com>
